==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Diabolic Gao''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Diabolic Gao is a powerful and versatile Uber. With outstanding DPS and [[Immune to Waves|wave immunity]], he is effective against most enemies as his DPS is higher than many others and his range is above-average, not to mention his massive health.

To add on all this, he deals [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|traitless]] enemies. Diabolic Gao will make dealing with enemies such as [[Master A.]] and [[R.Ost]] far easier, as long as he is protected by meatshields, since he can outrange them and does good damage. He will make [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]] pretty easy (provided you can deal with peons while not relying on [[Trolly Blogger]] to lure, or use other wave-immune meatshields in conjunction); he can also make [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]] easier since a level 40+ Shadow Gao does enough damage to knockback [[Mystic Mask Yulala|Yulala]] in one hit and [[Freeze|freeze]] him to make stalling much easier, which is normally extremely difficult. However, his freeze is a little too short to be significantly useful against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|traitless]] enemies and should be considered a bonus. Exceptions that will cause struggle for him are [[Kappy Jr.|Kappy]] and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Uril]].

Due to his effectiveness against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|traitless]] enemies and his gargantuan range, he is able to make the [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed/Manic]] stages much easier. Most of the stages have predominantly [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|traitless]] enemies, so he is usually effective against both the peons and the boss. Notable stages which he excels in include [[Dark Souls (Insane)|The Crazed Cat]], [[Absolute Defense (Insane)|The Crazed Tank]], [[Festival Gross (Insane)|The Crazed Gross]], [[Head Shaker (Insane)|The Crazed Cow]], [[Mammals? (Insane)|The Crazed Lizard]], [[Crazy Cats (Insane)|The Crazed Titan]] and their Manic counterparts. In that same sense, Diabolic Gao also makes [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening]] stages for most [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] and [[:Category:Monthly Events|Monthly Cats]] a cakewalk; provided proper meatshielding, of course, as he targets most of them, excluding [[Dark Lazer (Enemy)|Dark Lazer]], [[Beefcake Cat (Enemy)|Beefcake Cat]], [[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]], [[Nyalladin (Enemy)|Nyalladin]] and [[Kiss and Koi (Enemy)|Kiss and Koi]], who are either [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] or [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]].

